WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:02.000
Matthew 13

00:02.000 --> 00:07.360
That same day Jesus went out of the house and sat beside the sea,

00:07.560 --> 00:12.560
and great crowds gathered about him, so that he got into a boat and sat down.

00:13.120 --> 00:18.860
And the whole crowd stood on the beach, and he told them many things in parables, saying,

00:19.100 --> 00:25.900
A sower went out to sow, and as he sowed, some seeds fell along the path,

00:25.900 --> 00:31.080
and the birds came and devoured them. Other seeds fell on rocky ground,

00:31.460 --> 00:35.160
where they did not have much soil, and immediately they sprang up,

00:35.480 --> 00:40.360
since they had no depth of soil. But when the sun rose, they were scorched,

00:40.680 --> 00:46.120
and since they had no root, they withered away. Other seeds fell among thorns,

00:46.400 --> 00:52.240
and the thorns grew up and choked them. Other seeds fell on good soil and produced grain,

00:52.240 --> 00:55.860
some a hundredfold, some sixty, some thirty.

00:56.480 --> 00:59.280
He who has ears, let him hear.

01:01.240 --> 01:06.260
Then the disciples came and said to him, Why do you speak to them in parables?

01:06.900 --> 01:12.840
And he answered them, To you it has been given to know the secrets of the kingdom of heaven,

01:13.360 --> 01:18.520
but to them it has not been given. For to the one who has, more will be given,

01:18.700 --> 01:25.700
and he will have an abundance. But from the one who has not, even what he has will be taken away.

01:26.480 --> 01:30.940
This is why I speak to them in parables, because seeing they do not see,

01:31.240 --> 01:34.000
and hearing they do not hear, nor do they understand.

01:34.920 --> 01:39.140
Indeed, in their case the prophecy of Isaiah is fulfilled that says,

01:39.720 --> 01:44.780
You will indeed hear, but never understand, and you will indeed see, but never perceive.

01:45.560 --> 01:49.960
For this people's heart has grown dull, and with their ears they can barely hear,

01:49.960 --> 01:55.360
and their eyes they have closed, lest they should see with their eyes, and hear with their ears,

01:55.520 --> 01:55.880
and understand.

01:55.880 --> 01:59.320
Understand with their heart and turn, and I would heal them.

02:00.160 --> 02:05.140
But blessed are your eyes, for they see, and your ears, for they hear.

02:05.840 --> 02:10.000
For truly I say to you, many prophets and righteous people longed to see what you see,

02:10.280 --> 02:14.020
and did not see it, and to hear what you hear, and did not hear it.

02:14.940 --> 02:19.560
Hear then the parable of the sower. When anyone hears the word of the kingdom,

02:19.820 --> 02:25.400
and does not understand it, the evil one comes and snatches away what has been sown in his heart.

02:25.920 --> 02:30.660
This is what was sown along the path. As for what was sown on rocky ground,

02:31.040 --> 02:35.000
this is the one who hears the word and immediately receives it with joy.

02:35.320 --> 02:41.220
Yet he has no root in himself, but endures for a while, and when tribulation or persecution

02:41.220 --> 02:47.560
arises on account of the word, immediately he falls away. As for what was sown among thorns,

02:47.960 --> 02:52.640
this is the one who hears the word, but the cares of the world and the deceitfulness of riches

02:52.640 --> 02:55.280
choke the word, and it proves unfruitful.

02:55.920 --> 03:01.480
As for what was sown on good soil, this is the one who hears the word and understands it.

03:01.480 --> 03:07.880
He indeed bears fruit and yields in one case a hundredfold, in another sixty, and in another

03:07.880 --> 03:11.280
thirty. He put another parable before them, saying,

03:12.160 --> 03:16.940
The kingdom of heaven may be compared to a man who sowed good seed in his field.

03:17.680 --> 03:23.700
But while his men were sleeping, his enemy came and sowed weeds among the wheat and went away.

03:25.400 --> 03:32.940
And the servants of the master of the house came and said to him,

03:33.480 --> 03:38.720
Master, did you not sow good seed in your field? How then does it have weeds?

03:39.440 --> 03:45.160
He said to them, An enemy has done this. So the servants said to him,

03:45.480 --> 03:51.880
Then do you want us to go and gather them? But he said, No, lest in gathering the weeds

03:51.880 --> 03:55.180
you root up the wheat along with them. Let both grow together, and let one of them grow.

03:55.180 --> 03:55.380
And he said, No, lest in gathering the weeds you root up the wheat along with them.

03:55.400 --> 03:59.320
Let both grow together until the harvest. And at harvest time I will tell the reapers,

04:00.000 --> 04:05.980
Gather the weeds first, and bind them in bundles to be burned. But gather the wheat into my barn.

04:06.700 --> 04:12.720
He put another parable before them, saying, The kingdom of heaven is like a grain of mustard

04:12.720 --> 04:19.260
seed that a man took and sowed in his field. It is the smallest of all seeds, but when it

04:19.260 --> 04:25.180
has grown it is larger than all the garden plants and becomes a tree, so that the birds of the air

04:25.180 --> 04:30.260
come and make nests in its branches. He told them another parable.

04:31.200 --> 04:36.260
The kingdom of heaven is like leaven that a woman took and hid in three measures of flour,

04:36.740 --> 04:43.280
till it was all leavened. All these things Jesus said to the crowds in parables. Indeed,

04:43.380 --> 04:49.180
he said nothing to them without a parable. This was to fulfill what was spoken by the prophet.

04:49.180 --> 04:54.980
I will open my mouth in parables. I will utter what has been hidden since the

04:54.980 --> 05:01.180
foundation of the world. Then he left the crowds and went into the house, and his disciples came

05:01.180 --> 05:08.440
to him, saying, Explain to us the parable of the weeds of the field. He answered, The one who sows

05:08.440 --> 05:14.540
the good seed is the son of man, the field is the world, and the good seed is the sons of the

05:14.540 --> 05:20.360
kingdom. The weeds are the sons of the evil one, and the enemy who sowed them is the devil.

05:21.340 --> 05:24.960
The harvest is the close of the age, and the reapers are the ones who sow the good seed.

05:24.960 --> 05:31.260
Or angels. Just as the weeds are gathered and burned with fire, so will it be at the close of

05:31.260 --> 05:37.220
the age. The son of man will send his angels, and they will gather out of his kingdom all causes of

05:37.220 --> 05:43.680
sin and all lawbreakers, and throw them into the fiery furnace. In that place there will be weeping

05:43.680 --> 05:49.820
and gnashing of teeth. Then the righteous will shine like the sun in the kingdom of their father.

05:50.860 --> 05:53.200
He who has ears, let him hear.

05:54.960 --> 06:00.160
The kingdom of heaven is like treasure hidden in a field, which a man found and covered up.

06:00.600 --> 06:04.480
Then in his joy he goes and sells all that he has and buys that field.

06:05.320 --> 06:11.140
Again, the kingdom of heaven is like a merchant in search of fine pearls, who on finding one

06:11.140 --> 06:18.140
pearl of great value, went and sold all that he had and bought it. Again, the kingdom of heaven

06:18.140 --> 06:23.520
is like a net that was thrown into the sea and gathered fish of every kind. When it was full,

06:23.960 --> 06:24.940
men drew it ashore and threw it into the sea. He who has ears, let him hear.

06:24.960 --> 06:30.040
He who has nose, let him see. He who has tooth, let him wonder. He who has teeth licks his nose.

06:30.040 --> 06:35.520
When patient songs, it is easy with

06:36.240 --> 06:42.120
and throw them into the fiery furnace. In that place there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.

06:42.940 --> 06:47.080
Have you understood all these things? They said to him,

06:47.840 --> 06:54.540
Yes. And he said to them, Therefore, every scribe who has been trained for the kingdom of heaven

06:54.540 --> 06:54.940
is a people of God. He who has cheese, let him eat. He who has bread, let him buy bread. They say to him,

06:54.960 --> 06:56.560
is like a master of a house,

06:56.720 --> 07:00.120
who brings out of his treasure what is new and what is old.

07:01.880 --> 07:04.280
And when Jesus had finished these parables,

07:04.420 --> 07:05.400
he went away from there.

07:05.660 --> 07:08.320
And coming to his hometown, he taught them in their synagogue,

07:08.760 --> 07:11.080
so that they were astonished, and said,

07:11.300 --> 07:15.220
Where did this man get this wisdom and these mighty works?

07:15.980 --> 07:17.620
Is not this the carpenter's son?

07:18.180 --> 07:19.740
Is not his mother called Mary?

07:20.060 --> 07:23.700
And are not his brothers James and Joseph and Simon and Judas?

07:23.700 --> 07:26.340
And are not all his sisters with us?

07:26.580 --> 07:28.580
Where then did this man get all these things?

07:29.020 --> 07:30.800
And they took offense at him.

07:31.140 --> 07:32.320
But Jesus said to them,

07:32.700 --> 07:35.080
A prophet is not without honor,

07:35.520 --> 07:39.000
except in his hometown and in his own household.

07:39.860 --> 07:41.960
And he did not do many mighty works there,

07:42.220 --> 07:43.720
because of their unbelief.

